{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>Behold</b> — the Gaon [Saadia] said: the word מעיק, among the intransitive verbs, is figurative, for there is no strength to bear. And the sages of Spain say: it is a transitive verb, and מעיק is from the root of עקת רשע (Prov. 11:7), and it is like מציק." "<b>And beneath you</b> — in your place. The meaning: you shall be heavy and unable to flee, therefore what follows it."], :book :amos, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {0 "Resolved הגאון as Saadia per standard convention."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Amos -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/amos"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:17:50.683806172Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}